1
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:03,420
So, the power supply.

2
00:00:16,370 --> 00:00:17,430
Everything's assembled.

3
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:22,830
Now let's look at the current limiting, how the system works.

4
00:00:25,270 --> 00:00:26,290
Starting it up.

5
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,640
Ok, let's watch.

6
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:34,760
Current's at the minimum.

7
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:36,220
Adding more.

8
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,740
What's happening in the tank?

9
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:40,820
Basically nothing.

10
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:43,640
We add current.

11
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:55,540
This is 5 amps, the maximum current.

12
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:00,500
The system is handling super-saturated electrolyte.

13
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,960
You can see vigorous activity on

14
00:01:21,330 --> 00:01:24,750
the positive electrode and also on the negative one.

15
00:01:29,350 --> 00:01:30,650
Visible in the tank.

16
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:56,400
Without the current protection system, a short circuit would happen instantly in the super-saturated electrolyte and the power switches would blow right away.

17
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:59,220
Current is steadily limited to 5 amps.

18
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:08,960
Right now the power draw from the mains is 1.1 kilowatts.

19
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:33,530
The heat sink in this mode is about 50 degrees.

20
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,040
The cooling will be running.

21
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:40,760
Everything will be fine.

